summary: run memory configuration tests from Firmware Test Suite (fwts)
description: |
    Run fwts tests recommended [1] for testing Memory configuration

    ebda - EBDA region is mapped and reserved in memory map table.
    mcfg - MCFG PCI Express* memory mapped config space.
    mtrr - MTRR validation.
    dmar Check sane DMA Remapping (VT-d). 
    crs - Check PCI host bridge configuration using _CRS.
    maxreadreq - Checks firmware has set PCI Express MaxReadReq to a higher value on non-motherboard devices.

    1) https://wiki.ubuntu.com/Kernel/Reference/fwts#Which_Test_to_Run.3F
contact: Oliver Gutierrez <ogutierr@redhat.com>
component:
  - firmware
test: ./runtest.sh
framework: beakerlib
require:
  - beakerlib
duration: 60m
extra-summary: /kernel/firmware/fwts/memory-configuration
extra-task: /kernel/firmware/fwts/memory-configuration
